# Build artifacts
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Generated per-crate license manifest. The curated notices are tracked as
# THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md; this is the machine-generated long form, regenerated
# with `cargo about generate about.hbs > THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.html`.
/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.html

# Claude Code: everything under .claude/ is per-machine by default — permissions
# in settings.local.json, shell snapshots, session state — EXCEPT the shared
# subagent and skill definitions and the preview launcher, which are checked in
# so a fresh clone gets them.
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/launch.json

# The maintainer's private scratchpad. The tracked record is docs/roadmap.md.
/todo.md

# Codebase-review working notes — plan, fact sheet, ledger, index, snapshots.
# Findings that survive triage become §15 entries or roadmap items; the ledger
# itself is scaffolding and is not a project record.
#
# 🚨 Nothing here has a `git checkout` behind it, which is why CLAUDE.md's ban on
# scripted rewrites matters most for `review/findings.md` (23k lines) — a bad
# splice there is unrecoverable, not a revert.
/review/

# Design working files — mockups, handoff notes and their uploads. Local scratch
# for designing a feature, regenerated between sessions, never part of a commit.
/design/

# Throwaway probe binaries and their symbols. A `#[test]` that measures something
# is deleted once it has answered (CLAUDE.md, *Checking the chrome without a
# window*); a probe compiled to a binary leaves artifacts behind, and they are
# not a project record — the measurement belongs in §15.
/panicdetect.rs
/pd[0-9]
*.pdb

# Headless export scratch — `ondin export … -o out.svg` is the routine way to
# check rendering without a window (CLAUDE.md, *Checking rendering without a
# window*), and its output lands wherever the command was run.
/out.svg
/out.png
/out.json
/*.exe

# Editor / IDE folders
.vscode/
.idea/
.vs/
.zed/
*.iml

# Editor swap / backup files
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
